WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.490 --> 00:00:06.030
- We're tired.
- Stand up!
- [Together:] Fight back!
- Stand up!
- [Together:] Fight back!
- When Asians get attacked:
- [Together:] Stand up. Fight back!

00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:13.440
- We're tired of our cries

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:19.820
and anguish not being heard.
- Show me what community looks like!
- [Together:] This is what community looks like!
- Show them what community looks like!

00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:21.420
- We're tired of our pain

00:00:21.465 --> 00:00:22.395
being overlooked.
- Stand up!
- [Together:] Fight back!
- Stand up!
- [Together:] Fight back!

00:00:25.395 --> 00:00:26.735
- We're tired of keeping our heads

00:00:26.735 --> 00:00:28.535
down or not making any trouble

00:00:28.835 --> 00:00:29.765
when our elders are being

00:00:29.765 --> 00:00:31.564
assaulted, stabbed and killed.

00:00:31.955 --> 00:00:35.225
Wouldn't you be? The hate-fueled attacks

00:00:35.225 --> 00:00:37.565
on Asian Americans are disturbing, but

00:00:37.565 --> 00:00:40.144
why are we surprised? For many of us

00:00:40.144 --> 00:00:41.735
as Asian Americans in this country,

00:00:42.095 --> 00:00:43.805
we know what it feels like to be told

00:00:43.805 --> 00:00:45.545
we don't belong, that we're

00:00:45.545 --> 00:00:46.955
perpetually foreigners.

00:00:47.254 --> 00:00:48.275
And even though others try

00:00:48.275 --> 00:00:49.925
to minimize us to one entity,

00:00:50.325 --> 00:00:51.585
we represent so many different

00:00:51.585 --> 00:00:53.025
cultures, so many different

00:00:53.025 --> 00:00:55.005
backgrounds, so many different stories.

00:00:55.695 --> 00:00:57.585
What do you think happens next in a

00:00:57.585 --> 00:00:59.295
society where we've normalized

00:00:59.295 --> 00:01:01.835
xenophobia at the highest levels?
- Trump’s gonna f--k you.

00:01:05.405 --> 00:01:10.715
- [Offscreen:] You need to leave now.
- You need to leave.
- [Offscreen:] You do not talk to our guests like that.
- No, you need to leave.
- [Offscreen:] What’s wrong with you?
- [Offscreen:] You need to leave.
- F--king Asian piece of s--t.

00:01:10.715 --> 00:01:14.195
- [Offscreen:] Oh, my God.
- [Offscreen:] You need to leave right now.
- [Jeremy Lin:] People assign blame

00:01:14.195 --> 00:01:15.305
to those who don't deserve it.

00:01:15.785 --> 00:01:17.045
People are emboldened to

00:01:17.045 --> 00:01:18.725
vandalize Asian-owned businesses.

00:01:19.260 --> 00:01:20.880
People feel like it's OK to yell

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:22.710
at you in public based on your race.

00:01:23.160 --> 00:01:25.680
Normalizing hate speech stokes the flames

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:27.930
of racism and leads to an 84-year-old

00:01:27.930 --> 00:01:29.940
Thai grandfather lying helpless on the

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:32.460
streets of San Francisco, left to die after

00:01:32.460 --> 00:01:36.210
being attacked. 84. Years. Old. The next

00:01:36.210 --> 00:01:38.700
week, a 64-year-old grandmother assaulted

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:41.010
in San Jose and a Filipino American man

00:01:41.010 --> 00:01:42.930
slashed across the face in New York City.

00:01:43.470 --> 00:01:45.630
We're tired of this hateful violence.

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:46.950
We're tired of talking about it.

00:01:47.205 --> 00:01:48.045
But we're not done

00:01:48.045 --> 00:01:49.665
speaking out. Far from it.

00:01:49.995 --> 00:01:52.455
Listen to your AAPI [Asian American and
Pacific Islander] brothers and sisters.

00:01:52.605 --> 00:01:54.825
We must learn to love one another, to hear

00:01:54.825 --> 00:01:57.045
one another's anguish and actually care.

00:01:57.225 --> 00:01:58.455
Don't overlook the pain

00:01:58.485 --> 00:01:59.295
those around you are

00:01:59.295 --> 00:02:00.975
experiencing on a daily basis.

00:02:01.455 --> 00:02:03.705
Reach out to offer your support.

00:02:03.705 --> 00:02:05.955
To educate others. And let's put an end

00:02:05.955 --> 00:02:08.265
to this violence and hate, together.

